; Open table: a named rule of exactly TWO `* k => v` rows and nothing else, routed by CBOR wire
; major type. The typed (first) row claims exactly its key's single statically-known major; the
; catch-all (last) row sees only the complement.
;
; The three rules isolate the three things a snapshot of this shape has to show, and nothing else:
; the base composition, the `@duplicates preserve` flavor on both rows (two PairMaps with positional
; sidecars), and the NonEmpty (`{+ …}`) twin whose min-1 counts TYPED entries.
md = uint / text

; base: a bytes-keyed typed row (major 2) beside a uint/text catch-all (majors 0 and 3)
open_table = { * bstr => uint, * md => md }

; both rows under `@duplicates preserve`
open_table_dup = {
  * bstr => uint ; @duplicates preserve
  ,
  * md => md ; @duplicates preserve
}

; the NonEmpty twin: a restricted typed carrier, direct first-entry construction, and checked loose
; CBOR staging conversion
open_table_non_empty = { + bstr => uint, * md => md }
